From: Sam Day <me@samcday.com>
Subject: [PATCH] metainfo: mark prereleases with a tilde

The Fedora AppStream validator sorts the hyphenated prerelease versions
after the final 2.0.0 release. Use the tilde spelling already present in
upstream master so the chronological release list validates correctly.

--- a/data/me.gapixels.Megapixels.metainfo.xml
+++ b/data/me.gapixels.Megapixels.metainfo.xml
@@ -54,7 +54,7 @@
 				</ul>
                         </description>
                 </release>
-	        <release version="2.0.0-alpha2" date="2025-06-12">
+	        <release version="2.0.0~alpha2" date="2025-06-12">
                         <description>
 				<ul>
 					<li>Update to GNOME 47 runtime</li>
@@ -69,7 +69,7 @@
 				</ul>
                         </description>
                 </release>
-	        <release version="2.0.0-alpha1" date="2024-12-28">
+	        <release version="2.0.0~alpha1" date="2024-12-28">
                         <description>
                                 <p>
 					Pre-release version of Megapixels 2
